// Every place that OBTAINS `isSaas` and the question it is really asking.
//
// `isSaas` is a sanctioned client-side read (see the header of
// `deployment-profile.ts`), but "sanctioned" turned into "unexamined": three
// surfaces used it to answer questions that had named capabilities, and one of
// those had the capability read twelve lines away in the SAME file. The mode is
// the right thing to read only when the question genuinely IS the mode.
//
// So each entry names the question, and then either:
//   capability: "<name>"  the surface must actually read that capability — the
//                         gate checks it does, which is the machine-checkable
//                         form of "one question, one answer"
//   capability: null      no capability exists because the question really is
//                         about the mode itself; `reason` says why
//
// Enforced by `scripts/check-mode-disguises.mjs` (P4), bidirectionally: an
// unregistered read is stray, and an entry whose file no longer reads `isSaas`
// is stray too.
//
// SCOPE: obtain-sites only — `.isSaas` read off a context or branding object.
// Components handed `isSaas` as a prop are downstream of a decision already
// registered here, and the gate prints their count separately so this boundary
// is visible rather than implied.
{
  "surfaces": [
    {
      "file": "server/api/session-context.ts",
      "question": "What does the browser need to know about this deployment?",
      "capability": null,
      "reason": "Builds the wire payload. It is not deciding anything — it is transporting the mode so the client can, and the capabilities beside it come from `deploymentPayload`."
    },
    {
      "file": "app/components/Sidebar.tsx",
      "question": "Is there another workspace to switch to?",
      "capability": null,
      "reason": "The question really is the mode: only a platform has more than one workspace per identity, and the guard is paired with `portalBaseUrl` because the destination is the portal itself. No capability names this and inventing one would add a field with a single reader."
    },
    {
      "file": "app/components/sidebar/MobileDrawer.tsx",
      "question": "Is there another workspace to switch to?",
      "capability": null,
      "reason": "The mobile half of the same control as Sidebar.tsx. Deliberately identical — a fork here is how one of the two stops getting the next fix."
    },
    {
      "file": "app/routes/settings-hub.tsx",
      "question": "Should the Billing tile be offered?",
      "capability": "hasBilling",
      "reason": "Reads `deployment.hasBilling` first and falls back to `isSaas` only when the session payload predates that field. The fallback is the thing to remove once no cached session can be that old."
    },
    {
      "file": "app/routes/settings-communication.tsx",
      "question": "Whose Twilio credentials and inbound webhook does this tenant use?",
      "capability": "hasManagedCompliance",
      "reason": "Reads the capability for the managed-provisioning controls. The remaining `isSaas` reads are about WHICH inbound URL to display, which follows from who owns the number rather than from a capability."
    },
    {
      "file": "app/routes/settings-connected-apps.tsx",
      "question": "Is a platform-managed connection possible for this integration?",
      "capability": null,
      "reason": "Threads the mode into per-integration panels that each answer their own question. A capability per integration would be four fields with one reader each; the panels are where the specific questions live."
    },
    {
      "file": "app/routes/settings-usage.tsx",
      "question": "Does this deployment ever populate the inspections meter?",
      "capability": null,
      "reason": "The file states it: `caps` alone cannot tell standalone from a PAID saas tenant, because both are null. Only the mode separates them, and a standalone deploy never writes that counter — the card would sit at a permanent zero. This entry first claimed `hasUsageQuota` from assumption and the gate refused it, which is the check working."
    }
  ]
}
